 "notes": "Headline result: solar global fit (helioseismology + neutrinos) bound on hidden photons, chi*m < 1.8e-12 eV at 3 sigma (Sect. 4.4, abstract). Converted to kinetic mixing as chi = 1.8e-12 eV / m. Mass range 3e-5 to 8 eV taken from the range over which the paper states (Sect. 4.4, Fig. 11 'Sun-L (global)') the constraint is most stringent and over which the limit line is drawn; verified by digitising Fig. 11 (embedded raster in HPplot.pdf from the e-print): flat line at chi*m = 1.80e-12 eV spanning m = 2.9e-5 to 8.4 eV. The paper also derives an axion-photon bound g_agamma < 4.1e-10 GeV^-1 (3 sigma), but the hidden-photon bound is presented as the most restrictive/novel result. Stellar-emission bound: no dark-matter density assumption, no rescaling. Confidence level is 3 sigma (~99.7%), not 95%.",
